    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate change impacts on marine ecosystems",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the critical challenge of quantifying how rapidly and simultaneously multiple climate change drivers will emerge from natural ocean variability, which is a key uncertainty for predicting when marine ecosystems will face unprecedented stress and how much time is available for adaptation.",
    "method": "This study calculates the Time of Emergence for marine ecosystem drivers by analyzing a multi-model climate ensemble, defining emergence as the year when the long-term trend, estimated via generalized least-squares regression, persistently exceeds the natural variability derived from pre-industrial control simulations.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze climate model ensembles to determine how rapidly and where climate change trends in multiple environmental drivers of marine ecosystems will emerge from the background of natural variability under business-as-usual and mitigation scenarios.",
